<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Merksha Žarković</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1414</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Merksha Žarković was a Serbian nobleman who ruled the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlore">Valona</a> (Vlorë) in southern Albania from about 1396 until his death in 1414. He gained the city and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanine">Kanina</a> through his marriage to Ruđina, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balsa-ii">Balša II</a>, and held them against growing Ottoman pressure. After his death his widow ruled briefly before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> took Valona in 1417.</p></div>
